{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778553610,"nonce":"BI4WI88RDBi+JM7lx6KsiU81SlA=","title":"Auth event delivery lost during self-rebuild: ordering fix + SSE reconnect catch-up","message":"When a Mandible-repo auth request merges, the daemon broadcasts auth:resolved via SSE then immediately triggers a self-rebuild (npm build + process.exit). The channel server's SSE connection drops during the rebuild window, and the auth:resolved event is lost — the agent never gets notified.\n\n**Two fixes needed:**\n\n### Fix 1: Self-rebuild ordering (eliminates the problem at source)\n\nThe self-rebuild must not start until the auth:resolved event has been delivered. Currently in `src/auth-queue.ts`, the auth_hooks system detects `repo === \"mandible\"` and triggers the rebuild immediately after broadcasting.\n\n**Approach:** After broadcasting the auth:resolved SSE event for a self-rebuild request, add a short delay (1-2 seconds) before triggering the rebuild. This gives the channel server time to receive and process the event on localhost. The delay is negligible relative to the build time (several seconds).\n\n**More robust alternative:** Wait for the `markDelivered` POST from the channel server (which fires when it processes a matching auth:resolved event with `target_session_id` match) before triggering the rebuild. This is a positive acknowledgment rather than a timing guess. However, a simple delay is probably sufficient given localhost latency.\n\n### Fix 2: SSE reconnect catch-up (defense in depth)\n\nWhen the channel server's SSE connection to the daemon reconnects (after the 5s backoff in `createNotificationBridge`), it should run the same catch-up query as startup — fetch undelivered auth results and replay them as channel events. Currently, catch-up only runs once at process start (`runStartupCatchUp` in `channel-server/index.ts`).\n\n**Implementation:** In `channel-server/notifications.ts`, after a successful SSE reconnect (when `res.statusCode === 200` and backoff resets), call a catch-up function that queries `GET /api/inbox/undelivered?target_session_id=...\u0026conversation_id=...` and replays any results as channel events.\n\nThis covers daemon restarts from any cause (manual restart, crash, launchd respawn), not just self-rebuilds.","files":null}]}